---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Roblox Scripting Hub"
	description="A practical learning hub for Roblox Studio and Luau scripting."
	pubDate={new Date('October 20 2026')}
	heroImage="/blog-placeholder-about.jpg"
>
	<p>
		Roblox Scripting Hub is a focused place to learn Luau and Roblox Studio development through
		small, practical examples. The goal is simple: understand a concept, write the code, test it,
		and use it in a real game system.
	</p>

	<h2>What you'll find here</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Beginner-friendly Luau fundamentals</li>
		<li>Roblox Services, Instances, properties, and events</li>
		<li>Client/server patterns with RemoteEvents</li>
		<li>Reusable ModuleScripts and clean project structure</li>
		<li>Practical systems such as inventories, rounds, shops, and leaderboards</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>A good way to learn</h2>
	<p>
		Don't just copy scripts. Change one part, run the game in Studio, read the Output window, and
		figure out what changed. That feedback loop is one of the fastest ways to get comfortable with
		Luau.
	</p>

	<p>
		Roblox scripting uses Luau, a fast, gradually typed language derived from Lua. The official
		Roblox documentation is the best reference when you need exact API behavior.
	</p>
</Layout>
